WEBVTT

c01
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.230
Picture a team stuck with a slow, painful process.

c02
00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:14.690
Then a faster technology arrives, and they put it right on top of that process exactly as it is.

c03
00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:20.250
Does the problem go away? No. It gets locked in.

c04
00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:23.490
Now it just runs faster and at a bigger scale.

c05
00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:30.130
Back in 1990, Harvard Business Review published an article called Reengineering Work.

c06
00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:35.150
Its message was blunt. Don't automate. Obliterate.

c07
00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:38.490
In other words, don't speed up the old process.

c08
00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:40.750
Wipe it out and start again.

c09
00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:47.760
The idea is simple. If you put new technology on a broken process without taking it apart first,

c10
00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:50.590
you only speed up the inefficiency you already have.

c11
00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:56.530
The article was about ordinary computing, but it applies to AI just as well.

c12
00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:59.630
Let's see it in two real cases, decades apart.

c13
00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:07.070
Case one. The early 1980s. The accounts payable department of a U.S. car company.

c14
00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:13.690
500 people work there. A Japanese company runs the same department with about 100.

c15
00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:16.150
That's five times fewer.

c16
00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:19.150
And the U.S. company wants to close that gap.

c17
00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:23.950
So, before you see what they found, make the first call yourself.

c18
00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:27.550
So what did they find?

c19
00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:33.350
Mapping the process showed the real reason. Most of the work went into one thing,

c20
00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:36.230
matching three separate documents by hand.

c21
00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:40.290
Faster systems for the old process didn't close the gap.

c22
00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:44.230
Instead, they rewrote the process itself.

c23
00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:47.710
Now, payment is triggered straight from the receipt record.

c24
00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:49.590
No separate invoice.

c25
00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:54.530
According to reports, the headcount needed fell by about 75%.

c26
00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:02.590
Case two. A Swedish fintech between 2024 and 2025 according to public reports.

c27
00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:06.510
An AI agent starts handling its customer conversations.

c28
00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:10.290
About 2.3 million of them every month.

c29
00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:15.350
Reports put the drop in service load at the scale of about 700 service reps.

c30
00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:19.630
And handling time falls from about 11 minutes to under 2.

c31
00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:24.310
These figures come from company publications and media reports.

c32
00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:26.230
They're here for learning.

c33
00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:28.670
Not as proof that people should be replaced.

c34
00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:34.150
Then, by early 2025, the company starts hiring human service reps again.

c35
00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:39.290
Why? On simple requests, the AI did about as well as people.

c36
00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:43.710
But on complex ones, like disputes or personally difficult cases,

c37
00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:45.330
quality dropped noticeably.

c38
00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:48.190
So, what went wrong?

c39
00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:50.190
Decide before you hear it.

c40
00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:57.490
Management admitted it. Focusing too much on efficiency had hurt service quality.

c41
00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:00.230
The fix was a hybrid model.

c42
00:03:00.940 --> 00:03:05.750
AI handles the routine. A person steps in when empathy and judgment are needed.

c43
00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:11.830
Two cases, decades apart, completely different technology.

c44
00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:14.030
And the same lesson.

c45
00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:21.540
Process mapping is not a bureaucratic step. It's what separates a change that works from a change you have to fix

c46
00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:22.710
after the fact.

c47
00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:27.230
And notice, both stories are told in numbers.

c48
00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:31.390
Headcount, handling time, quality.

c49
00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:34.850
Without a number, nobody can check a change.
